  "report": "Initial stage, retained from the supplied prior findings: A04 and A08 independently repeat reported SS hydration within retailer reviews, respectively before makeup and alongside tretinoin/other actives. A09 separately reports hydration retention from Avant Guard plus SS, with no separable allocation. A03 reports SS stickier than Wave but continues using it; A04 reports lightweight, refreshing, fast-drying hydration. These descriptions do not establish universally nonsticky performance. A07's exact retrieved text remained “undefined...”; its testimony is unavailable. Earlier findings suffice for this update; earlier full records were not newly retrieved.\n\nUpdated stage: A13 adds a third credited retailer origin directly reporting SS hydration, including plump, hydrated skin after a 12-hour shift. This strengthens independently repeated reported hydration, not measured efficacy, prevalence or a known formula's performance. The 12-hour duration, reduced irritation/reactivity and oil production, and balancing dry sensitive cheeks against an oily T-zone without forehead congestion remain A13-specific. No direct SS hydration opposition is observed in the supplied evidence. Joint mask-serum retention remains one account, A09.\n\nSS texture remains mixed/conditional: A13 describes sticky, shiny, slick skin, with amount and willingness to appear shiny affecting daytime use. This aligns with A03 on experienced stickiness, but does not independently corroborate A03's exact Wave comparison; A03's independence is unavailable. A04's lightweight/fast-drying description remains material contrasting testimony, although those attributes can coexist with stickiness. No tested condition resolves the differences. A13's assertions about what most people will tolerate or when they should use SS are reviewer generalizations. A17 explicitly has never tried Experiment and only infers SS is thicker than Wave from stated glycerin percentages. It adds speculative texture comparison, neither first-hand SS texture nor hydration testimony; percentages and formula applicability are unverified.\n\nOther-product evidence cannot supply SS corroboration. A04/A10 retain Buffer Jelly overnight glow reports; A10's retained hydration concerns unspecified underlying products. A14 adds gifted Buffer Jelly experience after two uses: silky jelly-to-oil texture and soft skin without redness, irritation or clogged pores when mixed into nighttime moisturizer. Allocation within that combination is unresolved; anticipated post-dermaplaning suitability is untested. Its gift disclosure remains material despite metadata saying rewarded=false. A15 praises Plasma Wash's silky texture but reports inadequate cleansing, severe eye burning, less moisturized skin than a preferred glycerin cleanser and greater dryness after two washes despite multiple application methods. This contrasts with A04's favorable face-wash account, whose exact SKU is not established in the retained findings; it does not contradict SS hydration. A18 strongly praises Wave hydration but reports C.R.E.A.M failing overnight retention and pilling under sunscreen. A17's own C.R.E.A.M difficulties and desire for an oily extra layer provide qualified, same-thread alignment on moisturizer limitations, not SS evidence or an independently credited precise repeat of A18's overnight outcome. No cross-venue corroboration of the precise SS hydration or comparative texture proposition is established.\n\nBehavior: A04 narrates acquiring SS, Buffer Jelly for greater nighttime hydration/repair, face wash and mesh moisturizer; SS hydration alone cannot be assigned as the cause of all purchases. Refill metadata establishes no narrated repurchase. A03 continues SS despite stickiness, and A13 sometimes wears a pump during the day despite shine. A09 deducts one star for mask fit while praising retention. A14 reports receiving a free product and calls themself a convert, without a paid purchase or repurchase. A15 considered returning Plasma Wash but reports no completed return or remedy; suspected defect or misuse remains unresolved. A17 reports Experiment does not ship to their location and has not tried it. A18's rejection of C.R.E.A.M does not establish a completed return or switch. No focal completed repurchase or remedy is narrated.\n\nEngagement in both stages: all eight focal Junip accounts have 0 up-votes/0 down-votes; Reddit scores are A03=6, A17=7 and A18=10, each supplied as material_positive=false/not_interpreted. Observation times are unavailable. No material resonance credit is established. These metrics are not verified experiences, independent origins, prevalence or buying effects.\n\nContext outside focal counts: retained parent hillary_____k (t1_m7j6ppe, 2025-01-16; score 24) reports Black Friday acquisition of Regimen Lab Level, brighter/more even skin and strong future repurchase intention, not completed repurchase or SS performance. Skin_Fanatic (t1_m7jv3dh, 2025-01-17; score 2) asks about alternatives to untried C.R.E.A.M and expresses consideration, not experience. Engagement observation times are unavailable and resonance materiality is not established. The shared Reddit opener asks about Regimen Lab after advertising exposure; actor/time/engagement are unavailable. Context_f05862db0ee1dcb8c8c6 repeats A18 exactly and adds no account, origin or event. A03/A17/A18 share one Reddit thread; their independence is unavailable. Product-page/metadata contexts resolve targets and skin/variant information without donating testimony. SS formula versions remain unknown; A03's exact SKU is unknown. Counts below are updated focal source-account counts, not origin or event counts; initial counts were direct hydration 2, joint hydration 1, direct texture 2 and speculative texture 0.",
  "source_index": [
    {
      "key": "A03",
      "findings": "Retained prior evidence: Iusedtobealawyer, Reddit m7jkz2b, 2025-01-17, shared thread 1i30kik; independence unavailable. First-hand SS is stickier than Wave; continues SS because of believed higher glycerin content ('I think'). No direct hydration outcome or narrated purchase/repurchase. Exact SKU/formula unknown. Score 6, material_positive=false/not_interpreted; observation time unavailable. Parent hillary_____k's Level Serum acquisition, skin improvement and future repurchase intention concern another product."
    },
    {
      "key": "A04",
      "findings": "Retained prior evidence: Junip 7540631, credited customer 202931541, 2025-03-22. Direct SS hydration and lightweight, refreshing, fast-drying feel without clogged-pore feeling; suitable before makeup. Ordered after sister's introduction, then bought Buffer Jelly seeking greater nighttime hydration/repair, face wash and new mesh moisturizer. Buffer Jelly gave overnight glowing/clean-looking skin with a tiny amount despite initial thick/oily concern; face wash reportedly removed makeup, hydrated and ended breakouts, but exact wash SKU is not established here. Colorful packaging praised. Combo + Sensitive, SS Refill, verified buyer metadata supplies no narrated repurchase; formula unknown. Votes 0/0; observation time unavailable."
    },
    {
      "key": "A07",
      "findings": "Retained prior evidence: Junip 6884815, credited customer 122992865, 2025-01-17. Original and earlier exact retrieval both contain only 'undefined...'; hydration, texture and behavior testimony remain unavailable. SS First Time, Combo and verified-buyer metadata cannot replace testimony. Repeat retrieval/context is the same source, not another observation or origin. Formula unknown; votes 0/0, observation time unavailable. Excluded from all assertion counts."
    },
    {
      "key": "A08",
      "findings": "Retained prior evidence: Junip 4653282, credited customer 152576810, 2024-02-02. Age 51 with challenging skin; directly reports SS leaving skin hydrated alongside tretinoin/other actives. Conditional hydration testimony, without isolated efficacy, texture or explicit acquisition/repurchase/remedy consequence. Metadata: SS First Time, Combo + Acne Prone, verified buyer; formula unknown. Votes 0/0; observation time unavailable."
    },
    {
      "key": "A09",
      "findings": "Retained prior evidence: Junip 1866323, credited customer 55537943, 2022-12-09. Avant Guard plus SS reportedly locks in serum hydration; joint retention cannot be assigned separately to SS or mask and supplies no SS texture report. Very small head/nose fit complaint prompts one-star deduction alongside praise. Metadata: Avant Guard Small Head, Dry + Acne Prone; versions unknown. No narrated return, repurchase or remedy. Votes 0/0; observation time unavailable."
    },
    {
      "key": "A10",
      "findings": "Retained prior evidence: Junip 3515905, credited customer 97396127, 2023-07-21. Context resolves Buffer Jelly: small amount as final nighttime step retains hydration from unspecified products and yields glowing skin on waking. SS is unidentified, so no SS hydration/texture corroboration. Combo, verified-buyer metadata; formula unknown. No explicit buying, repurchase or remedy consequence. Votes 0/0; observation time unavailable."
    },
    {
      "key": "A13",
      "findings": "Junip 6685187, credited customer 231128721, 2024-12-06; updated minutes later, not a second event. Context identifies SS. Reports moisture retention/plump hydration through a 12-hour shift, improved appearance, less irritation/sensitivity and oil production, nourished dry sensitive cheeks with mild rosacea without oily-forehead congestion. Describes sticky, shiny, slick feel; sometimes wears a pump out, while suggesting smaller amounts/daytime tolerance and mainly nighttime use for others. Personal benefit coexists with texture burden; general claims about others are not additional testimony. No explicit purchase/repurchase/remedy. Metadata Oily + Sensitive, verified_buyer=false, rewarded=false; formula unknown. Votes 0/0; observation time unavailable."
    },
    {
      "key": "A14",
      "findings": "Junip 8950945, credited customer 344086099, published 2025-08-05, updated 2025-08-20; no distinct second use event established by update metadata. Explicitly received Buffer Jelly free for review and had used it twice; metadata rewarded=false does not erase disclosure. Describes jelly becoming fluid oil with silky slip; a drop in nighttime moisturizer reportedly yields soft skin without redness, irritation or clogged pores in a user with rosacea. Joint-use allocation unresolved; post-dermaplaning benefit is anticipated. Small bottle initially surprised them, but they assert 1 oz/reduced packaging and expect long life, not demonstrated duration. Calls themself an Experiment convert, without paid purchase/repurchase. No SS testimony. Metadata Combo + Acne Prone, unverified buyer; formula unknown. Votes 0/0; observation time unavailable."
    },
    {
      "key": "A15",
      "findings": "Junip 6567933, credited customer 210150638, 2024-11-04. Context identifies Plasma Wash. Praises silky texture but reports poor cleansing/no foam or disappearance across wet/dry skin, varying amounts and lathering methods; severe eye burning despite generally no eye makeup, less clean/moisturized feel than preferred glycerin cleanser, and greater dryness after two washes. Considered return, without completed return/remedy; defective product versus misuse unresolved, despite social-media praise. Two-star account; not SS opposition. Combo + Acne Prone, verified buyer metadata; formula unknown. Votes 0/0; observation time unavailable."
    },
    {
      "key": "A17",
      "findings": "Live_Rhubarb_7560, Reddit m7kd5t6, 2025-01-17, thread 1i30kik; independence unavailable. Explicit Experiment non-user because shipping unavailable locally; guesses Wave is thinner than SS from asserted 10% versus 30% glycerin. Counts only speculative SS texture, not hydration or use; percentages/formula applicability unverified. Likes Wave and hydrating serums, notes glycerin tackiness and wants larger bottles. Own C.R.E.A.M use is easier mixed with Wave; prefers tested Zerafite's more emollient, less pilling-prone feel, though thick/waxy, and agrees an oily extra layer can feel needed. Proposed ingredient/stability explanation is speculation. Reports over a month of tolerable Azelaic Advanced use, rejects Vit. X, finds Level fine but other routine sufficient, and likes Tabula Rasa; these are other-product testimony. Parent A18 is the same focal source, not extra corroboration; Skin_Fanatic's question adds no experience. Score 7, material_positive=false/not_interpreted; observation time unavailable."
    },
    {
      "key": "A18",
      "findings": "orchidmommy, Reddit m7j3q3q, 2025-01-16, thread 1i30kik; independence unavailable. Calls Wave the most hydrating thing used on their face. C.R.E.A.M reportedly retains moisture worse overnight than another moisturizer and pills under daytime sunscreen; favorable ingredients coexist with rejection ('wasn't for me'). No SS evidence or explicit completed return, repurchase or switch. Exact versions/comparator unknown. Context_f05862db0ee1dcb8c8c6 repeats this identical account; count once. Score 10, material_positive=false/not_interpreted; observation time unavailable."
    }
  ],
